cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PathSafe: Automated PHI Removal from Whole-Slide Pathology Images"
message: "If you use PathSafe in your research, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Soto
    given-names: Fernando
    affiliation: "McGill University Health Centre Research Institute, Department of Pathology"
repository-code: "https://github.com/DrSoma/PathSafe"
url: "https://github.com/DrSoma/PathSafe"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-03-17"
keywords:
  - pathology
  - anonymization
  - de-identification
  - whole-slide-image
  - PHI
  - HIPAA
  - digital-pathology
  - NDPI
  - SVS
  - DICOM
abstract: >-
  PathSafe is an open-source tool for removing Protected Health Information
  (PHI) from whole-slide image (WSI) files used in digital pathology. It
  supports all major scanner formats (NDPI, SVS, MRXS, BIF, SCN, DICOM,
  generic TIFF), implements Level IV anonymization as defined by Bisson et al.
  (2023), and generates verifiable compliance documentation. PathSafe provides
  both a graphical interface and a command-line tool for batch processing.
